===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|radishe}}, {{m|enm|redich}}, {{m|enm|radiche}}, {{m|enm|raddik}}, {{m|enm|radike}}, {{m|enm|redic}}, from {{inh|en|ang|redic}}, {{m|ang|rædic}}, from {{der|en|VL.|rādīce}}, the [[Appendix:Glossary#accusative case|accusative]] [[Appendix:Glossary#singular|singular]] of {{m|la|rādīx||[[root]] of a [[plant]]; radish}}; later influenced by {{der|en|xno|radich}}, {{m|nrf|radice}}, and {{der|en|frm|radice}} (modern {{cog|fr|radis}}), from Latin. Cognate with {{cog|da|reddike}}, {{m|da|ræddike}}, {{cog|it|radice}}, {{cog|dum|radic}}, {{cog|goh|ratih}}, {{m|goh|retih}} ({{cog|gmh|retich}}, modern {{cog|de|Rettich}}, {{m|de|Rettig}}), {{cog|osx|redik}} ({{cog|gml|rēdik}}, {{m|gml|reddik}}, {{m|gml|rētik}}, and other forms), {{cog|gmq-osw|rädikia}}, {{m|gmq-osw|rätikia}}, and other forms (modern {{cog|sv|rättika}}), {{cog|pt|radiz}}.

